{"uncertainty": 0.18, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: uart_tx reloads the data hold register while a frame is in flight", "summary": "Defect, from reading the RTL in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1]: the always block has an unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;` before the `case (state)`. It runs in every state, not only IDLE. The header comment in the same file is the only specification available here, and it says 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.'\n\nCausality: a start pulse during START, DATA or STOP overwrites `hold`. The DATA state then shifts out `hold[bit_idx + 1]` from the new value, so the remaining bits of the in-flight frame come from the new byte. The fault is the write to `hold` on the cycle that samples the mid-frame start. The failure appears later, when the receiver compares the whole byte.\n\nIncorrectness: the documented contract says a start while busy is ignored. The IDLE branch already loads `hold` correctly, so the line outside the case is redundant there and wrong everywhere else. The fix is to remove the unconditional load and keep the IDLE-only load. That fix also covers reloads during the START and STOP states.\n\nSupporting evidence: triage reproduced the regression failure as 1 of 4 checks failed, with $finish reached [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2] [run:run-0002]. VeriTriage's top hypothesis was 'Likely RTL bug', at only 30% confidence with a classification of unknown_failure [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. I treat that as one candidate to test, not as a conclusion. This analysis serves [requirement:req-d10c4df532].\n\nRanked hypotheses, each with the evidence that would refute it:\n(1) RTL bug, the reload-while-busy described above. Chosen. Refuted if the attached repro passes on this RTL, or if removing the unconditional load does not make its frame-1 check pass.\n(2) Testbench bug, meaning a wrong expected value. Rejected: the repro's expected values come from the documented 8N1 contract (0xA5 sent, 0xA5 expected), not from RTL output. The repro is built so that its checks pass on an RTL that ignores the mid-frame start. Refuted if a clean reference UART fails the same repro.\n(3) Infrastructure. Rejected as a primary cause: the triage run built and reached $finish with a counted verdict [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2], and the RTL defect alone explains a failing data check. Refuted only if a clean rebuild of an RTL without the reload line still fails.\n(4) Specification ambiguity. Rejected: the file's header clause directly fixes the behaviour of a start while busy. It would gain weight only if the project specification, which was not provided here, contradicted that comment.\n\nLimits: I did not read the content of triage_report.md or the triage testbench. I cannot confirm that the regression's failing check is the same reload scenario; that link is an inference."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse during an in-flight frame must be ignored", "summary": "Minimal self-checking repro for the defect in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-d10c4df532].\n\nStimulus: it sends 0xA5 and pulses start with 0x3C during data bit 3. It then sends 0x3C as a normal second frame.\n\nChecks (4 in total, all derived from the documented 8N1 contract and the 'start while busy is ignored' clause): frame 1 byte, frame 1 stop bit, frame 2 byte, frame 2 stop bit.\n\nExpected results: on the RTL under investigation, the frame 1 byte check should fail because bit 4 onward comes from 0x3C. On RTL that ignores the mid-frame start, all four checks should pass.\n\nIt reads nirmaan_nonce and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict just before $finish. A watchdog prints the verdict on timeout instead.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001", "run:run-0002"], "claims": ["The attached repro is expected to report 3 passed, 1 failed on the RTL under investigation and 4 passed on RTL that ignores a mid-frame start; this has not been simulated by me.", "Removing the unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;` line outside the case statement is expected to fix the defect.", "The regression failure seen in triage is presumed to stem from the same reload-while-busy behaviour; the triage report content was not available to confirm it."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Two things this analysis rests on but cannot confirm. First, the only specification available was the RTL file's own header comment; if a separate project specification defines start-while-busy differently, revisit the spec_ambiguity outcome. Second, the required independent review has not yet been recorded for this task; the existing review record [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.e1] covers the design fixture, not this analysis. Timing of the repro: CLKS_PER_BIT=4 and a 10 ns clock, so one bit is 40 ns. The receiver samples 18 ns after the start edge and every 40 ns after that, so no sample lands on a clock edge where tx changes."}

=== FILE: tb/uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v ===
// Repro: a start pulse while a frame is in flight must be ignored
// (8N1 UART, LSB first). Expected values come from that contract.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module uart_tx_reload_repro_tb;
    localparam integer CPB = 4;
    localparam integer BIT = CPB * 10;   // 10 ns clock period

    reg        clk = 1'b0;
    reg        rst = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data = 8'h00;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    reg     done = 1'b0;

    reg [7:0] rx1, rx2;
    reg       stop1, stop2;

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CPB)) dut (
        .clk(clk), .rst(rst), .start(start), .data(data),
        .tx(tx), .busy(busy)
    );

    // Receive one frame: wait for the start edge, sample mid-bit.
    task recv;
        output [7:0] b;
        output       s;
        reg    [7:0] t;
        integer      i;
        begin
            @(negedge tx);
            #(BIT/2 - 2);
            for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
                #(BIT);
                t[i] = tx;
            end
            #(BIT);
            s = tx;
            b = t;
        end
    endtask

    task check;
        input            cond;
        input [8*48-1:0] msg;
        begin
            if (cond) passed = passed + 1;
            else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("CHECK FAILED: %0s", msg);
            end
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "unset";

        repeat (4) @(posedge clk);
        @(negedge clk) rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(negedge clk);

        // Frame 1: send 0xA5, pulse start with 0x3C during data bit 3.
        fork
            recv(rx1, stop1);
            begin
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'hA5;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
                repeat (16) @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'h3C;   // must be ignored
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
            end
        join
        check(rx1 == 8'hA5, "frame1 byte is A5 despite mid-frame start");
        check(stop1 == 1'b1, "frame1 stop bit is 1");
        if (rx1 != 8'hA5)
            $display("frame1 received %h, expected a5", rx1);

        wait (!busy);
        repeat (4) @(negedge clk);

        // Frame 2: a normal frame of 0x3C.
        fork
            recv(rx2, stop2);
            begin
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'h3C;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
            end
        join
        check(rx2 == 8'h3C, "frame2 byte is 3C");
        check(stop2 == 1'b1, "frame2 stop bit is 1");

        wait (!busy);
        @(negedge clk);
        done = 1'b1;
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

    initial begin
        #100000;
        if (!done) begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK FAILED: timeout");
            $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
            $finish;
        end
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===

